--[[
	FLAMETHROWER  |  Created by DuaKNo & Monkey      (LocalScript, no server script needed)

	SETUP
	1. Toolbox -> Inventory/Models -> add the flamethrower (asset 8083772765) to the game.
	   Put the Tool in StarterPack. Roblox then clones it into every player's Backpack.
	2. Put THIS script in StarterPlayer > StarterPlayerScripts as a LocalScript.
	That's all. It finds the tool by name ("flame"), so keep "Flamethrower" in its name.

	If the model has its own Scripts / LocalScripts inside, delete them. This script
	handles flames, fuel, burning and blood itself and they would fight each other.

	Held:    the tool's own Handle/Grip is used, so the avatar holds it normally.
	Tank:    a banded back tank + hose is added to your avatar (needed for the fuel nozzle; the lite version
	         has the tank and hose too, just no fuel).
	Burning: skin goes red, scorched, then charred. NPCs bleed and the blood dries.
	Fuel:    hold the prompt at the pump, the nozzle hooks onto your tank, then CLICK the
	         nozzle (or the PUMP button) over and over to fill the tank.
	Menu:    only shows while the flamethrower is equipped. Drag it by the title bar, resize it from the
	         bottom-right corner, minimize it to a small square with the _ button or the M key.
	Version: a small draggable card asks which version to run before anything loads (the game behind it
	         stays clickable). Full version = all features.
	         Flamethrower only = flamethrower, shoulder hold, NPC burning and death. Plus ground fire, black marks,
	         napalm, blue flames, fire spread and the back tank + hose. No fuel, heat, begging or blood.
	Sounds:  upload the files from Flamethrower_Sounds.zip (Creator Hub -> Audio), then paste the
	         asset IDs into CFG.SOUNDS (a plain number works). README.txt in the zip lists which is which.
	Hold:    shoulder stance. The gun is held out from your right shoulder in a fixed pose that does not
	         shake with walking, and only tips up/down with where you aim. Shift lock turns on by itself
	         while the flamethrower is equipped (Shift toggles it).
	Cursor:  a crosshair shows in the middle of the screen while shift lock is on.
	Flames:  menu toggles: blue flames, fire spread (burning NPCs / ground fire ignite whatever is close) and
	         napalm (full version: sticky fire that stays on the ground and sets NPCs on fire when they walk in it).
	         Fire never just switches off, it dies down slowly (CFG.FADE_TIME).
	Re-run:  executing the script again first removes the previous copy (its menus, HUDs, rig and NPCs).
	Kills:   NPCs die for real: the script claims network ownership of the NPC and sets Humanoid.Health to 0
	         (same method as the car spawner). Ownership only works while the flamethrower is equipped.
	Chat:    NPC lines use Roblox's own bubble chat.
	No store tool found -> a built-in wand is built instead (CFG.FALLBACK_BUILTIN).
]]

